{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Look, the day is still long.</b> Since he saw them lying down — as though he supposed they wanted to gather the flocks home and would graze no more — he said to them: Look, the day is still long; that is, if you are hired men, you have not completed the day's labor, and if the animals are your own, even so — ״it is not the time to gather the livestock, etc.״ (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:02.323641600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}